(6056405, 891127, 10785, '<td valign="top">I like your choice for this challenge. I think everyone''s grandparents had this portrait hanging on the wall somewhere in the house. I like your twist on the portrait too with the urban theme. It really shows how far removed current society is from the spiritual foundations of our forefathers. A Comic Book and a TV replaces the bible and the can of food and crackers depicts just how far removed from the land we are. I would love for you to redo this to appear closer to the portait rather than with the HDR look. A nice black background and some softer focus would be great. At any rate. I enjoyed your photo.</td>', 'I like your choice for this challenge. I think everyone''s grandparents had this portrait hanging on the wall somewhere in the house. I like your twist on the portrait too with the urban theme. It really shows how far removed current society is from the spiritual foundations of our forefathers. A Comic Book and a TV replaces the bible and the can of food and crackers depicts just how far removed from the land we are. I would love for you to redo this to appear closer to the portait rather than with the HDR look. A nice black background and some softer focus would be great. At any rate. I enjoyed your photo.', '2010-06-14 21:13:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6056406, 890325, 112828, '<td valign="top">This really is more of a "in the style of" rather than an interpretation of a famous photograph....  <br/> <br/>Sorry, but this is a 5, and that kills me because this is wonderful.. You did a great job here, but I''m afraid that I don''t think this really follows any work of William Wegman''s that I can find or think of..<br/> <br/>Please correct me if I am wrong.</td>', 'This really is more of a "in the style of" rather than an interpretation of a famous photograph....   Sorry, but this is a 5, and that kills me because this is wonderful.. You did a great job here, but I''m afraid that I don''t think this really follows any work of William Wegman''s that I can find or think of.. Please correct me if I am wrong.', '2010-06-14 21:13:04.000000', NULL, 1),
