(6064168, 891009, 67237, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ErinKirsten:</b></div><hr/><i> ...... Go Jawbones!!  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>After seeing the Jawbones profile page, I think it would be more appropriate to say Go Gyaban!  JK :-) you are all very talented<br/> <br/>Gyaban joined DPC less than 4 months ago, got a red on his 1st free study entry, then a blue... and (so far) has grabbed 5 ribbons during DPL2<br/>5 out of his team''s top 6 percentiles are his<br/>Portraiture, indoor setup, outdoor setup, landscape, color, b&amp;w, he''s done it all with tons of talent<br/>..... what an outstanding performance!<br/>I don''t know if that is a record for DPL, but I am sure it will hardly be matched in the future.<br/>Huge congrats Christophe!!!<br/> <br/>ETA: I say he should be banned for DPL3 :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-06-21 04:16:16.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by ErinKirsten: ...... Go Jawbones!!    After seeing the Jawbones profile page, I think it would be more appropriate to say Go Gyaban!  JK :-) you are all very talented Gyaban joined DPC less than 4 months ago, got a red on his 1st free study entry, then a blue... and (so far) has grabbed 5 ribbons during DPL25 out of his team''s top 6 percentiles are hisPortraiture, indoor setup, outdoor setup, landscape, color, b&w, he''s done it all with tons of talent..... what an outstanding performance!I don''t know if that is a record for DPL, but I am sure it will hardly be matched in the future.Huge congrats Christophe!!! ETA: I say he should be banned for DPL3 :-)', '2010-06-21 05:00:00.000000', '2010-06-21 05:16:16.000000', 0),
