(6064751, 891119, 117285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> very good idea, the setup is a little too "clean" to convey it </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks and I agree, this particular foreground theme was a last minute addition when my first idea didn''t pan out.  It should have been as gritty as the moment itself</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: very good idea, the setup is a little too "clean" to convey it   Thanks and I agree, this particular foreground theme was a last minute addition when my first idea didn''t pan out.  It should have been as gritty as the moment itself', '2010-06-21 16:04:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6064766, 891009, 100335, '<td valign="top">Amazing, inspiring, and well deserved win, you''ve made a fan out of me! Looking forward to seeing more of your work!</td>', 'Amazing, inspiring, and well deserved win, you''ve made a fan out of me! Looking forward to seeing more of your work!', '2010-06-21 16:24:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6064767, 891119, 117285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jutilda:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m really shocked.  This got a 10 from me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I appreciate that. Not to knock the other "migrant mother" image in this challenge but I felt that I executed this representation much more precisely yet I can understand how my soft focus must have not sat well with the voters.  Well at least it chops up to a good learning experience. I should have left the mother in focus. Seems like i fooled some into believing it was the original print out of focus in the background and not a recreation.  Is it not obvious that those are mannequins and not real children?  That actually part of the reason I defocused the mother and children, because I couldn''t stand the inaccurate details.  Now in hindsight I wish i would have built on this and made the image much more artistically stylized and used the mannequins to that advantage.</td>', 'Originally posted by Jutilda: I''m really shocked.  This got a 10 from me.   I appreciate that. Not to knock the other "migrant mother" image in this challenge but I felt that I executed this representation much more precisely yet I can understand how my soft focus must have not sat well with the voters.  Well at least it chops up to a good learning experience. I should have left the mother in focus. Seems like i fooled some into believing it was the original print out of focus in the background and not a recreation.  Is it not obvious that those are mannequins and not real children?  That actually part of the reason I defocused the mother and children, because I couldn''t stand the inaccurate details.  Now in hindsight I wish i would have built on this and made the image much more artistically stylized and used the mannequins to that advantage.', '2010-06-21 16:25:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6064772, 891009, 118315, '<td valign="top">Above and beyond.  Congratulations.</td>', 'Above and beyond.  Congratulations.', '2010-06-21 16:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6064773, 891072, 75713, '<td valign="top">Well there is a saying that everyone has a twin somewhere on the planet and you found Jim''s twin.  Not only is the resemblance remarkable, so is the lighting, the pose, the post processing .. I will stop now :) but you get the picture ... and the ribbon.  Congratulations!</td>', 'Well there is a saying that everyone has a twin somewhere on the planet and you found Jim''s twin.  Not only is the resemblance remarkable, so is the lighting, the pose, the post processing .. I will stop now :) but you get the picture ... and the ribbon.  Congratulations!', '2010-06-21 16:35:45.000000', NULL, 0),
